an/repo; forge -R world/paper-repo issue close 6 2>&1|tail -1; cd /hutian/paper-repo && git fetch -q origin document; git show origin/document:dev/built-from; git show origin/document:dev/document.pdf > /tmp/d.pdf; pdfinfo /tmp/d.pdf|grep Pages; pdftotext -f 1 -l 1 /tmp/d.pdf - | head -70"]], "output": "```console\nClosed #6\n4c7c1727065c9882fea75e938fe60a5136870907\nPages:           24\n000\n001\n002\n003\n004\n005\n006\n007\n008\n009\n010\n011\n012\n013\n014\n015\n016\n017\n018\n019\n020\n021\n022\n023\n024\n025\n026\n027\n028\n029\n030\n031\n032\n033\n034\n035\n036\n037\n038\n039\n040\n041\n042\n043\n044\n045\n046\n047\n048\n049\n050\n051\n052\n053\n054\n\nHow much shorter can a prediction-powered interval be?\nHeadroom over PPI++ when labels, unlabeled data and predictor are fixed\n\nAnonymous Authors1\nbeled sample, a large unlabeled one and the predictor’s\noutputs into a confidence interval that is valid whatever the\npredictor’s quality, and PPI++ tunes a scalar weight on the\npredictor to make the interval as short as the linear use of\nthe predictor allows (Angelopoulos et al., 2023a;b). The\nwidth of the interval is what the analyst pays for with labels,\nso the practical question after validity is how much shorter\nit can be.\n\nAbstract\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "3c603d3d-0a60-5237-964d-caaf80a62f03", "at": 1795691770.8188667, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84667, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "2f06ccd6-b422-5f2c-b675-a87be91fbcf2", "at": 1795691770.8568819, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84668, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permissio