", "kind": "model.request", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "completed", "label": "model → completed", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "model request → completed in 2.2s (instruction ✓, activation ✓) [max_tokens 128000, output_config.effort high, thinking.display summarized, thinking.type adaptive]; gateway set thinking.display; called Bash ×1; tokens in 67,791 (cached 67,060, 99%, written 729 (1h 729, 5m 0)) out 101; requested claude-sonnet-5-5; served claude-sonnet-5-5 ×1", "model": {"requests": 1, "attempts": [{"outcome": "stream-ended", "category": "completed", "seconds": 2.1695327379275113, "served": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"]}], "probes": {"instruction_present": true, "activation_present": true}, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": null, "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 729, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 729, "cached_input": 67060, "input": 67791, "output": 101}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 112551, "other": 423, "system": 40100, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 45266}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 212737}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "c8d31075-e369-545a-86dc-626781679568", "at": 1795691773.8854063, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84731, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "b2407674-6509-5a76-9d17-43b3302cadaf", "at": 1795691773.8908212, "until": 1795691774.4286861, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84732, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01KdNcffeo7DDpAr3d5YSnxe", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/paper-repo && git checkout -q origin/dev; sed -n 1,40p paper/sections/abstract.tex | cut -c1-1500", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/paper-repo && git checkout -q origin/dev; sed -n 1,40p paper/sections/abstract.tex | cut -c1-1500"]], "output": "```console\nPrediction-powered inference (PPI) turns a fixed predictor into a valid confidence interval for a mean, and PPI++ is its strongest form when the labels, the unlabeled records and the predictor are given. We ask how much shorter such an interval can be without changing any of the three. Classical semi-supervised theory gives a variance floor; we write the exact gap between PPI++ and it, which vanishes if and only if the regression of the outcome on the prediction is affine, and a break-even label count above which learning a calibrated control variate from the same labels pays. On the nine datasets of the \\texttt{ppi-python} package, at the reference label count ($n=500$; $200$ on the smallest pool) a cross-fitted interval that chooses between PPI++ and calibrated alternatives is within $1\\%$ of the width of the strongest valid PPI++ baseline (the package's or an unclipped variant) on every dataset (a label saving of at most $1.2\\%$), and an estimated floor is at most $3.3\\%$ shorter than the package's interval. The one gain over the package, $13\\%$ of the labels at $n=100$ on \\texttt{gene\\_expression}, comes from its clip of the estimated tuning weight to $[0,1]$, not from calibration, and disappears against the unclipped PPI++. With $100$ labels or fewer learning costs width: the chosen interval is a median $1.9\\%$ wider. Where the regression is far from affine (synthetic populations) savings reach $47\\%$ of the labels, and the break-even formula holds where its test is poss\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "844fbdf0-8157-5133-a215-028e9eefb8aa", "at": 1795691774.3663592, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84735, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "a671f02f-e664-506d-a172-5f983cc12d86", "at": 1795691774.3850327, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84736, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "cc0b7296-9c2f-58a1-a0bd-6b830ef4a366", "at": 1795691774.3881454, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84737, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "118d5a35-cf7a-5659-8a92-b8394d35e36e", "at": 1795691774.542874, "until": 1795691778.579251, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84741, "layer": "worker", "category": "model", "kind": "model.request", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "6a0878a57b569e597e6704b6533f8ab9", "trust": "s